                          Installation


                            /X 2.xx


-Modify your custom-commands and add the following line:

*req        XM050Doors:request/request

^         ^    ^
|         |    |_ Or wherever you put Requester.
|         |
|         |___ Notice the "X" Request is an XIM door!
|
|______ The name to run.

-Copy all files in BBS/doors/request/ to doors:request/






                             /X 3.xx


-Copy the icon BBS/Commands/Conf<x>cmd/req.info to BBS:Commands/Conf<x>cmd 
 where the x stands for the number of the requestconference.

-Copy all files in BBS/doors/request/ to doors:request/

-Add ~CC_req to your downloadmsg.txt in the request-conf




                    Tooltypes in request.info

==============================>X<=============================

BULLETIN_PATH=bbs:conf6.request/bull50.txt
^
+- Path to bullfile that will be created.

==============================>X<=============================

BULLETIN_HEAD=doors:request/bulletinhead.txt
^
+- Path to the head of the bulletin.

==============================>X<=============================

BULLETIN_TAIL=doors:request/bulletintail.txt
^
+- Path to the tail of the bulletin

==============================>X<=============================

CHARACTER=[36m|[0m
^
+- This is the character between colums in the bulletin.

ANSI codes can be used in tooltypes.
To write the escape character, press lamiga+ctrl+esc... 

==============================>X<=============================                                                              

MESSAGE_PATH=bbs:Conf6.Requests/MsgBase/
^                                      ^
|                                      + do NOT forget the last /
|
+- Path to the MSgBase where the door will put your mezzez.

==============================>X<=============================

MESSAGE_REQUEST_TXT=bbs:conf6.request/message.txt
^
+- Path and filename of the asciitext that will be used to create letter

==============================>X<=============================

MESSAGE_REQUEST_TO=EALL
^
+- To who do ya want to write the requestmessages

==============================>X<=============================¶

MESSAGE_REQUEST_SUBJECT=Request!
^
+- A string that will be put as subject to requestletters that will be created.

==============================>X<=============================

DELETE_ACCESS=250
^
+- The minimum access for deletionoverride.

==============================>X<=============================

REQUEST_DATA=s:req.data
^
+- The path and filename to the datafile. 

==============================>X<=============================








                 How to create a Messageletter


This is an ordinary asciifile use the following codes in the letter:

°UserName          Prints out the username instead
°Location          Prints out the location instead
°FileDescription   Prints out the filedescription instead
°UserComment1      Prints out the first line from the usercomment
°UserComment2      Prints out the second line from the usercomment

Exampel follows:

=========================================================>cut<=============

          UserName:   °UserName 
      UserLocation:   °Location 

   FileDescription:  °FileDescription

                                User Comment:
 (|-------|-------|-------|-------|-------|-------|-------|-------|-------|--)
> °Usercomment1
> °Usercomment2

=========================================================>cut<=============





